WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:22.162
Gerald heard the crunching sound of something walking along the gravel path.

2
00:00:22.163 --> 00:00:26.311
An enormous stone dinosaur was lumbering toward him!

3
00:00:26.312 --> 00:00:32.553
"It can't see me," Gerald told himself. "I'm not afraid."

4
00:00:32.554 --> 00:00:38.629
As the dinosaur passed, Gerald reached out and touched it.

5
00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:43.281
The moving statue turned toward him, but Gerald was suddenly afraid.

6
00:00:43.282 --> 00:00:46.043
He took off and ran toward the castle.

7
00:00:46.044 --> 00:00:51.314
Gerald spotted the open window of the treasure room.

8
00:00:51.315 --> 00:00:57.621
He climbed up to the window, using the vine that clung to the castle.

9
00:00:57.622 --> 00:01:01.954
Once inside the room, he turned and looked outside.

10
00:01:01.955 --> 00:01:07.626
In the moonlight he could see that the goat-boy statue was back underneath the willow tree.

11
00:01:07.627 --> 00:01:10.071
Nothing moved outdoors.

12
00:01:10.072 --> 00:01:14.180
"This is very strange. Maybe I'm dreaming."

13
00:01:14.181 --> 00:01:20.346
He shut the window and removed the key from the door lock.

14
00:01:20.347 --> 00:01:26.548
Outside the treasure room, he locked the door again.

15
00:01:26.549 --> 00:01:35.354
Then he put the key in its hiding place and crept along the corridor.

16
00:01:35.355 --> 00:01:41.156
He wandered through the castle, opening doors and feeling safe because he was invisible.

17
00:01:41.157 --> 00:01:45.022
At last he came to a door with light shining under it.

18
00:01:45.023 --> 00:01:53.242
Gerald hesitated for a moment before flinging open the door.

19
00:01:53.243 --> 00:01:58.905
"Hey!" cried a voice from within the room.

20
00:01:58.906 --> 00:02:03.594
Gerald flattened himself against the wall as a man sprang to the door.

21
00:02:03.595 --> 00:02:07.256
The man flashed a lantern into the corridor.

22
00:02:07.257 --> 00:02:09.717
"It's all right," the man said.

23
00:02:09.718 --> 00:02:12.389
"It was only the door swinging open."

24
00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:16.800
"Close that door!" growled another voice.

25
00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:18.660
That was fine with Gerald.

26
00:02:18.661 --> 00:02:20.821
He had already seen enough.

27
00:02:20.822 --> 00:02:25.332
A gang of burglars was taking silver out of two large chests!

28
00:02:25.333 --> 00:02:30.611
They had picked the door's lock and now their tools lay on the floor.

29
00:02:30.612 --> 00:02:33.821
"Hurry up!" one burglar said.

30
00:02:33.822 --> 00:02:36.227
Gerald ran down the corridor.

31
00:02:36.228 --> 00:02:39.143
What should he do?

32
00:02:39.144 --> 00:02:41.038
He hurried outside.

33
00:02:41.039 --> 00:02:46.857
Through a window he saw Mabel and her aunt having a delicious supper.

34
00:02:46.858 --> 00:02:50.331
He took out his notebook and pencil and wrote:

35
00:02:50.332 --> 00:02:52.553
You know the room where the silver is?

36
00:02:52.554 --> 00:02:55.562
Burglars have picked the lock and are stealing the silver.

37
00:02:55.563 --> 00:02:58.396
Send a man for the police. A friend

38
00:02:58.397 --> 00:03:01.675
P.S. This is not a joke.

39
00:03:01.676 --> 00:03:05.748
Gerald looked hungrily at Mabel's supper.

40
00:03:05.749 --> 00:03:09.111
He tied the note to a rock with his shoelace.

41
00:03:09.112 --> 00:03:12.675
Then he threw the rock through the window.

42
00:03:12.676 --> 00:03:16.580
Mabel and her aunt jumped up, shrieking in surprise.

43
00:03:16.581 --> 00:03:22.199
Mabel picked up the rock, and her aunt read the note.

44
00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:27.791
"Nonsense!" said the aunt. "Of course this is a joke."

45
00:03:27.792 --> 00:03:34.105
"Please," wailed Mabel. "Send for the police like he says."

46
00:03:34.106 --> 00:03:37.796
"Like who says?" snapped her aunt.

47
00:03:37.797 --> 00:03:41.527
"Whoever wrote the note," moaned Mabel.

48
00:03:41.528 --> 00:03:45.888
Gerald realized he must do something more.

49
00:03:45.889 --> 00:03:48.312
"Send for the police at once,"

50
00:03:48.313 --> 00:03:51.328
he called out in his manliest voice.

51
00:03:51.329 --> 00:03:54.517
"You'll only blame yourself if you don't."

52
00:03:54.518 --> 00:03:59.487
"Auntie, please wake Bates right away," begged Mabel.

53
00:03:59.488 --> 00:04:05.980
"Oh, all right." Mabel's aunt finally went off to get one of the male servants.

54
00:04:05.981 --> 00:04:09.801
Bates was not happy to be woken up.

55
00:04:09.802 --> 00:04:14.137
But after reading the note, he went to the police on his bicycle.

56
00:04:14.138 --> 00:04:19.625
By the time the police arrived, the burglars and the silver were gone.

57
00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:22.862
Gerald had a long night.

58
00:04:22.863 --> 00:04:32.606
It was late when he crept into bed, exhausted and cold as stone.

59
00:04:32.607 --> 00:04:37.729
The next morning Eliza the maid went into Gerald's room.

60
00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:44.957
"Wake up! It's a beautiful day!"

61
00:04:44.958 --> 00:04:50.606
She opened the curtains at one window and turned to call him again.

62
00:04:50.607 --> 00:04:53.082
But his bed was empty.

63
00:04:53.083 --> 00:04:55.421
"I wonder where he is."

64
00:04:55.422 --> 00:04:58.333
She opened the curtains at the other window.

65
00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:03.257
But this time when she turned around, she screamed.

66
00:05:03.258 --> 00:05:10.981
Gerald was lying in the bed!
